%% One cluster run from submission to pulled results.
%% Shown in docs/project/running.md.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor You
  participant Submit as submit.sh<br/>(your machine)
  participant Login as Login node
  participant Slurm
  participant Job as job.sbatch<br/>(compute node)
  participant Pull as pull.sh<br/>(your machine)

  You->>Submit: submit.sh #lt;experiment#gt; #lt;command#gt;
  Submit->>Submit: record commit and uncommitted changes (patch)
  Submit->>Login: create runs/#lt;experiment#gt;/#lt;run id#gt;/
  Submit->>Login: copy code/ and provenance/, update the code mirror
  Submit->>Login: write run.json (status: submitted)
  Submit->>Slurm: sbatch, with every option from defaults.sh and .env
  Slurm-->>Submit: job id
  Submit-->>You: run id and job id, then returns
  Note over Submit,Login: if any step fails, the run folder is removed

  Slurm->>Job: start, when a node is free
  Job->>Job: check the environment matches the run's uv.lock
  Job->>Job: record host, GPU, versions in run.json (status: running)
  Job->>Job: check the GPU can run this PyTorch (GPU jobs)
  Job->>Job: run the command, from the run's frozen code
  alt the command ends
    Job->>Job: status: completed, or failed
  else 2 minutes before the time limit, or scancel
    Slurm->>Job: TERM signal
    Job->>Job: stop the command, status: timeout, or canceled
  end
  Job->>Job: record end time and exit code in run.json

  You->>Pull: pull.sh #lt;experiment#gt;
  Pull->>Login: copy the run folders, without code/ and checkpoints/
  Login-->>Pull: outputs/runs/#lt;experiment#gt;/#lt;run id#gt;/
